__Concept:__

Efficiency of a machine = **Useful work output / Work input** = dfrac{W{ₒᵤₜ}}{W{ᵢₙ}} (often expressed as a percentage).

Given

Load (W) = 1 {kN} = 1000 {N}

Load displacement = 100 {mm} = 0.100 {m}

Effort (E) = 40 {N}

Effort displacement = 5 {m}

Calculation

Useful work output:

W{ₒᵤₜ} = {Load}times{load displacement} = 1000×0.100 = 100 {J}

Work input:

W{ᵢₙ} = {Effort}times{effort displacement} = 40×5 = 200 {J}

Efficiency:

eta = dfrac{W{ₒᵤₜ}}{W{ᵢₙ}} = dfrac{100}{200} = 0.5 = 50\%

(Alternatively, Mechanical Advantage = MA=dfrac{1000}{40}=25, Velocity Ratio = VR=dfrac{5}{0.1}=50, so eta=dfrac{MA}{VR}=dfrac{25}{50}=0.5=50\%.)
